{
  "id": "inhibition-of-return",
  "term": "inhibition of return",
  "definition": "Inhibition of return is a tendency for people to respond more slowly to a target when it appears in a location that was cued before, compared with a new location. In the supplied source, this effect is described as being influenced by memory retrieval and contextual similarity between successive targets.",
